  "summary": "Superconducting qubit platforms now target non-sinusoidal junction transport, from higher harmonics to gate-tunable Andreev spin states.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is treating Josephson junction current-phase transport as a design variable rather than assuming an ideal sinusoidal relation. A proposal for noise-protected superconducting qutrits uses the second harmonic of the current-phase relation in three-junction loops with altermagnetic elements. A study of Al/AlOx/Al tunnel junctions examines non-ergodic area scaling of Andreev transport against the sinusoidal ideal. Gatemon work reports in-situ ternary InAsSb/Al nanowire junctions with gate tunability over GHz and coherent control, with T1 of about 0.2-1 us. Planar Ge Josephson junctions show gate-tunable spin splitting for Andreev spin qubits that is independent of junction width, unlike InAs. What is new is the range of materials platforms and deliberate departures from conventional junction behavior. All four items are preprints, and their scope and maturity differ.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
